[62.152276, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[62.15254, "o", "1. **Likelihoods**: We use the Poisson log-likelihood for each channel $i$: \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[62.152587, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[62.152856, "o", "   $$\\log P(k_i | \\lambda_i) = -\\lambda_i + k_i \\log(\\lambda_i) - \\log(k_i!)$$\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[62.152904, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[62.153358, "o", "   where $\\lambda_i$ is either the background-only expectation ($B_i$) or the signal-plus-background expectation ($\\mu S_i + B_i$).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[62.153412, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[62.153461, "o", "> "]
[62.153729, "o", "2. **Test Statistic**: The observed likelihood-ratio test statistic is computed as:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[62.153777, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[62.154105, "o", "   $$q = -2 \\log \\frac{L(\\text{data} | S+B)}{L(\\text{data} | B)} = -2 (\\log L_{sb} - \\log L_b)$$\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[62.154153, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[62.1542, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
